//! Elements are 11 limbs of 61 bits (unsaturated, 671 bits of
//! storage) in Montgomery form with `R = 2^671`. Arithmetic results
//! are lazily reduced to `[0, 2p)`; encoding and comparison reduce
//! fully. `2^610` divides `p + 1`, so the Montgomery reduction folds
//! each emitted low limb `v` back in as `v * 17 * 2^54` at limb
//! position 10.
